MTPLX
-----
crates/lisa-mlx/src/shaders/qwen4/qsa/{prefill,prefill_header,select,select_header}.metal
and crates/lisa-mlx/src/models/qwen4/qsa.rs are adapted from MTPLX:
https://github.com/youssofal/MTPLX
Copyright the MTPLX authors. License: Apache License, Version 2.0.
https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
The source operations are mtplx/kernels/qsa_prefill_flash.py and
mtplx/kernels/qsa_indexer_select.py. The sparse-attention design and
block-selection tie-break (score - block_id * 1e-12) follow that project.
The local host dispatch, tensor layout and some kernel details are adapted.

Candle
------
The following sources derive from candle-metal-kernels 0.11.0:
https://github.com/huggingface/candle

- shaders/common/elementwise/elementwise_binary.metal: src/metal_src/binary.metal
- shaders/common/elementwise/cast.metal: src/metal_src/cast.metal
- shaders/common/elementwise/select.metal: src/metal_src/ternary.metal
- shaders/common/data/indexing.metal: src/metal_src/indexing.metal
- shaders/common/matmul/dense_gemm.metal: src/metal_src/mlx_gemm.metal
- shaders/common/matmul/dense_gemv.metal: src/metal_src/gemv.metal

All paths above are relative to crates/lisa-mlx/src/. These are vendored
kernel sources with local integration and adaptations, without a Candle runtime
dependency. Copyright (c) 2023-2025 Hugging Face and the contributing authors.
Candle is distributed under MIT or Apache-2.0; LISA's existing attribution uses
MIT. The GEMM/GEMV sources also retain their original Apple MLX MIT attribution
(Copyright (c) 2023-2024 Apple Inc.).

DS4
---
DS4-derived GLM kernels live under crates/lisa-mlx/src/shaders/glm53/ and in
common/attention/ds4_flash_attn.metal, common/matmul/glm53_*.metal and
common/elementwise/glm53_moe_grouped_swiglu_weight.metal. Associated Rust
bindings and GLM execution code adapt DS4's shape gates and scheduling to
LISA's runtime, with legacy MLX affine storage and native GGUF block views.

Upstream: https://github.com/antirez/ds4
Reference revision: b4e3faf5262b21db94ec309cf321640ff1eed460
Source families include metal/dense.metal, metal/glm53_bf16.metal, metal/dsv4_misc.metal,
metal/moe.metal and metal/flash_attn.metal.
Copyright (c) 2026 The ds4.c authors.
Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors.
Copyright (c) 2023 DeepSeek.
License: MIT. The full notice is retained in:
crates/lisa-mlx/src/shaders/common/attention/ds4_flash_attn.LICENSE
crates/lisa-mlx/src/shaders/common/elementwise/ds4_glm53_moe_swiglu.LICENSE

The DeepSeek V4.1 GGUF port under crates/lisa-engine/src/models/deepseek41/
and crates/lisa-mlx/src/{models,shaders}/deepseek41/ uses DS4 revision
b3f50180ec2c7324892be1f50bc83555ccb8d5e7. It adapts the tokenizer, Engram
hash/read scheduling, hyper-connections, cache quantization, sparse attention,
index selection and routed/shared experts to LISA's Rust runtime. Source
hashes and local adaptations are recorded beside each shader. The full MIT
notice is in crates/lisa-mlx/src/shaders/deepseek41/LICENSE.
The native V4.1 renderer and DSML parser in crates/lisa-serve/src/deepseek41.rs
port ds4_server.c and ds4_tool_text.h from that same revision. Their original-C
test oracle identity is in deepseek41_provenance.json; the full MIT notice is
retained in crates/lisa-serve/src/LICENSE-DS4.
The reference builder under crates/lisa-bench/reference/deepseek41/ extracts
that pinned DS4 graph and GGML CPU decoders into an external build directory.
Generated upstream code retains these licenses; adapter identities and compiler
commands are recorded in its build manifest.

The native GLM GGUF path under models/glm53/gguf and shaders/glm53/gguf_*
uses DS4 revision b3f50180ec2c7324892be1f50bc83555ccb8d5e7. Original Q2_K and
Q4_K helpers are included in shaders/deepseek41/iq.metal. Shared native GGUF
BPE and GLM4 split rules live in lisa-engine/src/core/gguf_tokenizer.rs and
gguf_glm4.rs. Adjacent JSON files record source and adapter identities.

GGML packed-weight extensions
----------------------------
The GGUF block decoders and codebooks under crates/lisa-gguf/src/
derive from ggml-org/llama.cpp revision
ca3d5a3e10d53f7ea672cb9b6178faca3e2807bc. The IQ1_M, IQ2_XS and Q5_K
Metal arithmetic helpers in shaders/deepseek41/iq.metal derive from revision
7071ba378afa96dcd69c41e1ec2b4912364dbee4; the IQ2_XXS path retains DS4's
helper. These adapters retain the original GGML block bytes and do not
requantize the checkpoint to MLX affine storage.
Upstream: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors. License: MIT.
Full notices and provenance are retained in crates/lisa-gguf/src/LICENSE-GGML
and crates/lisa-mlx/src/shaders/deepseek41/LICENSE-GGML, with provenance.json
alongside the sources.

MLX-Serve media implementations
-------------------------------
The native vision processors/encoders and FLUX.2 pipeline under
crates/lisa-engine/src/models/{vision,flux2}/ adapt operation order and model
layout from https://github.com/ddalcu/mlx-serve
Revision: 6c4306145b7331f6b962b97e145fd9ac46e9e14a
Copyright (c) 2026 David Dalcu. License: MIT (full text below).
LISA supplies its own Rust execution, bounded attention and convolution storage,
request isolation, image decoding, HTTP handling and AppKit integration.

The LayerNorm source common/attention/layer_norm.metal comes from MLX revision
1f8e74e3f12f31365464a6867c6579f0e9b29d85,
mlx/backend/metal/kernels/layer_norm.metal. The utils include and explicit
instantiation list are omitted because LISA supplies them at JIT assembly.
Original SHA-256: 2d243f5abea7353929f9bc838ceb5a98e52a452dfc29609ad4d5974447ea689f

Black Forest Labs FLUX image inference
--------------------------------------
The native FLUX 3 implementation under crates/lisa-engine/src/models/flux3/
adapts the transformer, text-encoder contract, VAE layout and flow-map schedule
from https://github.com/black-forest-labs/flux-3-image-klein
Revision: bfc8889a4497f846416f253a3972a1941ac698b9.
Copyright 2026 Black Forest Labs, Inc. License: Apache-2.0.
The full license is retained in crates/lisa-engine/src/models/flux3/LICENSE.
LISA changes execution to Rust/Metal, stages model loading, bounds attention and
convolution scratch, and uses its bundled text encoder for prompt expansion
with a compact adaptation of the reference's external-LLM caption guide.
FLUX.2 Klein 9B dimensions and encoder taps were checked against the official
https://github.com/black-forest-labs/flux2 reference at
50fe5162777813d869182b139e83b10743caef15. MLX tensor bytes are retained.
Model weights carry their own licenses, separate from inference source code.

